  "query_preview": "..\n(Sunday night through Wednesday)\nIssued at 955 PM CDT Wed Oct 21 2026\n\nThe upper ridge will breaking down Sunday night into Monday/Tuesday\nas the southwest U.S. ejects into the Plains and OH Valley. The \nsouthern tail of this wave will move through Tuesday into \nWednesday, but the airmass will too dry to support precipitation. \nThe surface ridge will remain in place, but pressures will be \nfalling as it weakens. Temperatures in upper 60s to lower 70s on \nMonday under the influence of the wedging ridge will warm into the\nlower to middle 70s Tuesday and Wednesday. Lows will be in the \nlower to middle 40s over the weekend into Monday morning, warming \ninto the middle 40s to around 50 by Wednesday and Thursday \nmornings.",
